  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_018: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat; acc=0.619) establishes that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation + concat fusion is the strongest architecture. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as PCA (a linear method). Since RNA is the dominant signal source (RNA-only multiprofile achieves 0.591 vs image-only 0.208), the choice of RNA representation is a high-impact, unexplored design axis. Config_030 swaps only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 (a learned nonlinear single-cell embedding) while holding all other settings at their best-known values. This cleanly isolates whether a deep learned RNA representation outperforms linear PCA in this pipeline. If scvi significantly improves over PCA, it opens a high-value exploitation path; if it performs similarly, we can rule out RNA encoder as a lever and redirect budget toward image encoder or other dimensions. This is the most informative single experiment under the limited budget because it tests the largest unexplored design choice on the primary signal modality."
}

